<title>SYRIA: Syria buys 13,000 t raw sugar at dlrs 290.</title>
<headline>Syria buys 13,000 t raw sugar at dlrs 290.</headline>
<dateline>DAMASCUS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria's General Foreign Trade Organisation for Chemicals and Foodstuffs (GEZA) has bought 13,000 tonnes of raw sugar at dollars 290 per tonne, a GEZA spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>He told Reuters the sugar, bought from France's Lurico, should be delivered between April 15 and May 15.</p>
<p>He said a tender to buy 13,000 tonnes of white sugar was cancelled as price offers did not meet GEZA's conditions.</p>
